{
  "tema": 8327,
  "slug": "presente-uar",
  "titulo": "Conjugate -uar verbs in the present: actuar, continuar",
  "subtitulo": "Actúo, continúas, continuamos: the accent jumps onto the u.",
  "foto": "t05.jpg",
  "regla": "Verbs in -uar like actuar and continuar take an accent on the u in the present except nosotros: actúo, actúas, actúa, actuamos, actúan.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Verbs ending in **-uar** take a **written accent on the u** in most forms of the present."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "actuar",
            "continuar"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "actúo",
              "continúo"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "actúas",
              "continúas"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "actúa",
              "continúa"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "actuamos",
              "continuamos"
            ],
            [
              "ustedes, ellos",
              "actúan",
              "continúan"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Why? In the infinitive the stress is on the end (**actu-AR**). In **yo**, **tú**, **él** and **ellos**, the stress moves to the **u** (**ac-TÚ-o**). The accent breaks the vowel pair so the **u** can carry the stress. In **nosotros** the stress stays at the end, so there's no accent."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Other verbs like this: **evaluar**, **graduarse**, **situar**, **acentuar**. Watch out: **averiguar** doesn't do this."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the **u** stands up and takes a bow, **actúo**. Only **nosotros** keeps it sitting."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Alex ==actúa== en el teatro; es el protagonista.",
              "en": "Alex performs at the theater; he's the lead."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los músicos ==actúan== cada sábado en el bar.",
              "en": "The musicians perform every Saturday at the bar."
            },
            {
              "es": "Después del intermedio ==continúa== la obra.",
              "en": "The play continues after the intermission."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los trabajadores ==continúan== con la huelga.",
              "en": "The workers are continuing the strike."
            },
            {
              "es": "Creo que nos perdimos. ¿==Continuamos== o descansamos?",
              "en": "I think we're lost. Shall we keep going or rest?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Ustedes ==continúan== haciendo ruido.",
              "en": "You keep making noise."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
